So visit the course page link given below in the description and take
the first step towards career growth with the data science course.

2625
02:49:10,048 --> 02:49:12,608
你是梦想成为一名数据科学家的人吗？
Are you someone who dreams of becoming a data scientist?

2626
02:49:12,782 --> 02:49:16,688
继续观看，因为我们将向你展示数据科学在现实世界中是如何运作的。
Keep watching because we are going to show you how data science works in the real world.

2627
02:49:16,848 --> 02:49:18,848
认识一下 Alex，他是一名数据科学家。
Meet Alex, He's a data scientist.

2628
02:49:19,008 --> 02:49:24,036
让我们快速看看他在处理供应链优化项目时的一天是怎样的。
Let's take a quick look at what his day looks like as he works on a supply chain optimization project.

2629
02:49:24,208 --> 02:49:28,128
解决任何问题的第一步就是理解问题本身。
The first step in solving any problem is understanding the problem itself.

2630
02:49:28,288 --> 02:49:31,328
为此，Alex 与运营团队开会。
And for this, Alex gets in a meeting with the operation team.

2631
02:49:31,488 --> 02:49:35,328
他提出问题，深入挖掘，并找出究竟需要解决什么问题。
He asks questions, digs deeper, and figures out what exactly needs to be solved.

2632
02:49:35,568 --> 02:49:41,568
他创建了可操作的问题，例如目标是降低成本、缩短交付时间，还是更好地管理库存。
He creates action-able questions such as is the goal to reduce cost, improve delivery time, or manage inventory better.

2633
02:49:41,808 --> 02:49:44,608
他还会检查系统目前是否存在任何问题。
He also checks if there are any current issue with the system.

2634
02:49:44,768 --> 02:49:48,928
一旦业务目标明确，Alex 就会进入下一步，即数据获取。
Once the business goal is clear, Alex moves to the next step, which is data acquisition.

2635
02:49:49,088 --> 02:49:53,648
这意味着收集正确的数据，让机器从中学习并做出智能建议。
This means collecting the right data for machine to learn from and make smart suggestions.

2636
02:49:53,808 --> 02:50:00,048
把它想象成烹饪，就像烹饪需要正确的食材一样，数据科学项目也需要正确的数据。
Think of it like cooking, just as you need the right ingredient for cooking, similarly,
you need the right data for a data science project.

2637
02:50:00,128 --> 02:50:05,168
而这个从不同来源收集有用信息的过程就叫数据获取。
And this, the process of gathering useful information from different sources is called data acquisition.

2638
02:50:05,408 --> 02:50:12,048
Alex 从库存系统、订单管理平台、仓库日志以及第三方供应商的 API 中收集数据。
Alex collects data from inventory system, order management platform, warehouse logs, and third-party suppliers, APIs.

2639
02:50:12,208 --> 02:50:16,368
没错，寻找正确的数据需要时间、耐心和对细节的关注。
And yes, finding the right data takes time, patience, and attention to detail.

2640
02:50:16,528 --> 02:50:20,768
数据收集完成后，Alex 进入下一步，即数据准备。
So once the data is collected, Alex moves to the next step, which is data preparation.

2641
02:50:20,928 --> 02:50:24,208
原始数据以其自然形式存在时是非常混乱且无结构的。
Raw data in its natural form is very messy and unstructured.

2642
02:50:24,368 --> 02:50:28,128
在数据结构化之前，你无法直接进入分析或建模。
You can't jump into analysis or modeling until the data is structured.

2643
02:50:28,288 --> 02:50:31,008
而且一旦结构化，工作还没结束。
And once it is structured, the job is still not done.

2644
02:50:31,168 --> 02:50:34,208
我们还需要对它进行清洗、转换和组织。
We still need to clean it, transform it, and organize it.

2645
02:50:34,368 --> 02:50:42,048
Alex 在这里需要检查空行、重复条目、缺失的交付时间戳，并确保数据集中没有不一致的地方。
Alex here needs to check the empty row, duplicate entries, missing delivery timestamps,
and ensure that there are no inconsistency in the data set.

2646
02:50:42,208 --> 02:50:45,888
这一步通常是整个过程中最耗时的部分。
This step is often the most time-consuming part of the entire process.

2647
02:50:46,048 --> 02:50:46,288
为什么？
Why?

2648
02:50:46,448 --> 02:50:51,728
因为在这里，你要确保拥有解决实际业务问题所需的正确信息。
Because here you are making sure that you have the right information needed to solve the actual business problem.

2649
02:50:51,888 --> 02:50:58,128
数据清洗并结构化之后，Alex 开始进行探索性数据分析，也就是 探索性数据分析。
So once the data is clean and structured, Alex moves on to exploratory data analysis or EDA.

2650
02:50:58,208 --> 02:51:01,728
这是一个非常关键的步骤，他需要识别出真正重要的特征。
A very critical step where he identifies the features that really matter.

2651
02:51:01,968 --> 02:51:03,248
但为什么这很重要呢？
But why is this important?

2652
02:51:03,488 --> 02:51:05,968
假设你要预测送货时间。
So let's say you're trying to predict delivery time.

2653
02:51:06,242 --> 02:51:11,568
像产品成本、支付方式或 ID 这样的特征有帮助吗？那些基本上只是订单详情。
What features like product cost, payment mode, or ID help, those are basically the order details.

2654
02:51:11,648 --> 02:51:13,888
它们对送货时间没有任何影响。
They have no influence on the delivery time.

2655
02:51:13,968 --> 02:51:17,248
所以把它们留在我们的数据科学流程中就没意义了。
So keeping them in our data science process doesn't make any sense.

2656
02:51:17,408 --> 02:51:21,568
如果我们把它们包含进来，可能会削弱模型或者引入不必要的噪声。
If we include them, we might weaken the model or introduce unnecessary noise.

2657
02:51:21,808 --> 02:51:28,128
这就像是为一个人做饭，你不会把冰箱里的所有东西都拿出来，只需要你需要的准确配料。
Think of it like cooking for one person, you don't grab everything from the fridge, just the exact ingredients you need.

2658
02:51:28,288 --> 02:51:30,528
这样你就不会做得过头或者浪费时间。
That way you don't overcook or waste time.

2659
02:51:30,768 --> 02:51:33,488
探索性数据分析 能帮助你在数据科学项目中做到同样的事情。
TDA helps you do the same in a data science project.

2660
02:51:33,648 --> 02:51:38,682
只关注相关的特征，这样你的模型才会高效、准确且符合特定用途。
Focus only on relevant features so that your model is efficient, accurate, and purpose-built.

2661
02:51:39,088 --> 02:51:42,688
接下来是第 5 步，也就是准备数据科学模型。
Next comes the step 5, where the data science model will be prepared.

2662
02:51:42,928 --> 02:51:45,088
Alex 手头已经有了清洗好的数据。
Alex already have a clean data at hand.

2663
02:51:45,168 --> 02:51:50,368
现在他用最适合该业务问题的机器学习算法来训练这些获取到的数据。
Now he trains this acquired data with machine learning algorithm that fit best to the business problem.

2664
02:51:50,528 --> 02:51:55,248
他可以应用随机森林、K-means 聚类和线性回归等模型。
He can apply model like random forest, k-means clustering, and linear regression.

2665
02:51:56,368 --> 02:51:59,328
他训练这些模型并评估它们的性能。
He trains these model and evaluates their performance.

2666
02:51:59,408 --> 02:52:03,168
为此，他使用了准确率评分或混淆矩阵等指标。
To do that, he used metrics like accuracy score or confusion metrics.

2667
02:52:03,328 --> 02:52:09,008
这些指标能帮助 Alex 了解模型在训练完成后，在测试数据上的表现如何。
These metrics help Alex understand how well models are able to perform on test data after they are trained.

2668
02:52:09,168 --> 02:52:14,688
Alex 通常首选 Python，不过根据需求，他也会使用 R 或 SQL。
Alex usually prefer Python for this, though he also uses R or SQL depending on the requirement.

2669
02:52:14,848 --> 02:52:18,208
现在你可能会觉得，既然有了准确的模型，任务就完成了。
Now you might think that we have accurate model that means the job is done.

2670
02:52:18,368 --> 02:52:19,088
嗯，并不是这样的。
Well, not true.

2671
02:52:19,248 --> 02:52:22,768
Alex 现在需要再次向业务相关方展示他的发现。
Alex now needs to present his finding to business stakeholders again.

2672
02:52:22,928 --> 02:52:27,888
Alex 再次与业务团队会面，用清晰直观的方式传达他的发现。
Alex meets with the business team again to communicate his finding in a clear, straightforward way.

2673
02:52:28,128 --> 02:52:37,488
他使用 Tableau、Power BI 和 Excel 来创建可视化报告和仪表盘，
这些内容对于业务负责人来说是直观易懂的。
He uses tools like Tableau, Power BI, and Excel to create visual reports and dashboard,
which are self-explanatory and easy to understand for business leader.

2674
02:52:37,728 --> 02:52:42,288
一旦 Alex 获得批准，他就会进入下一步，也就是模型部署。
Once Alex gets the approval, he then moves to the next step, which is deploying the model.

2675
02:52:42,448 --> 02:52:49,248
部署完成后，Alex 通过仪表盘监控实时指标，并继续微调模型的性能。
Once it is deployed, Alex monitors real-time matrix using dashboard and continues fine-tuning the model's performance.

2676
02:52:49,408 --> 02:52:52,288
这就是 Alex 完成一个数据科学项目的过程。
And this is how Alex completes a data science project.

2677
02:52:52,448 --> 02:53:02,768
每个数据科学项目通常从业务问题、数据获取开始，然后经过
数据准备、探索性数据分析、建模、报告，最后以部署结束。
Every data science project generally starts from business problem, data acquisition, and then come stages such as data preparation,
EDA, modeling, reporting, and end with deployment.

2678
02:53:02,928 --> 02:53:07,648
通过 Alex 的旅程，我们现在对整个数据科学项目生命周期有了清晰的了解。
With Alex journey, now we have a clear picture of entire data science project lifecycle.

2679
02:53:07,808 --> 02:53:11,888
那么让我们继续往下看，看看数据科学如今是如何改变各行各业的。
So let's move forward and look at how data science is transforming industry today.

2680
02:53:12,240 --> 02:53:16,960
在零售业，它能帮助预测需求，并在高峰时期防止缺货。
In retail, it helps forecast demand and prevents talkouts during peak scale periods.

2681
02:53:17,200 --> 02:53:21,802
在物流领域，它能找到更具成本效益的配送规则并减少燃料消耗。
In logistic, it finds some cost efficient delivery rules and reduces fuel uses.

2682
02:53:22,000 --> 02:53:26,080
在人力资源领域，它能帮助预测员工流失情况并提高团队留存率。
In HR, it helps predict employee turnover and improve team retention.

2683
02:53:26,480 --> 02:53:30,720
在医疗保健领域，它能加速诊断并助力个性化治疗。
In healthcare, it accelerates diagnosis and powers personalized treatment.

2684
02:53:31,040 --> 02:53:33,280
数据科学家可以承担多种角色。
A data scientist can take on many roles.

2685
02:53:33,440 --> 02:53:40,000
你可以成为业务分析师、机器学习工程师、数据工程师，或者是专门从事供应链的数据科学家。
You can become a business analyst, machine learning engineer, data engineer, or a specialized supply chain data scientist.

2686
02:53:40,240 --> 02:53:48,000
在2025年，根据你的技能和行业不同，平均年薪在10万美元到17万美元之间。
In 2025, the average salary ranges from $100,000 to $170,000 depending on your skills and industry.

2687
02:53:48,174 --> 02:53:53,280
而在印度，根据 Glassdoor 的数据，他们的收入在70万卢比到180万卢比之间。
Whereas in India, they earn between 7 lakh rupees to 18 lakh rupees as per glass tool.

2688
02:53:53,360 --> 02:53:55,920
那么，你准备好开始你的数据科学家之旅了吗？
So are you ready to begin your journey as a data scientist?

2689
02:53:56,080 --> 02:54:01,520
如果准备好了，就从今天开始吧，因为数据世界只会越来越大，它需要像你这样的人。
If yes, start today because the world of data is only getting bigger and it needs people like you.

2690
02:54:01,840 --> 02:54:05,920
无论你手头有没有计算机科学学位都没关系。
It doesn't matter whether you have a computer science degree in hand or not.

2691
02:54:06,190 --> 02:54:10,532
无论你过去有没有编程经验也没关系。
Neither does it matter whether you have programming experience behind your back or not.

2692
02:54:10,800 --> 02:54:16,868
说到在数据科学领域找工作，唯一重要的是你是否掌握了相关技能。
When it comes to getting a job in data science domain, all that matters is whether you have got the skills.

2693
02:54:17,280 --> 02:54:25,156
确实，对于以前的许多求职者来说，获得数据科学技能只能通过硕士或博士学位来实现。
It's true that for many aspirants back in the day, acquiring data science skills was only possible with master's and PhD degrees.

2694
02:54:25,518 --> 02:54:33,860
考虑到数据科学需要精通四个不同的领域，比如统计学、编程、机器学习和商业洞察。
Considering the fact that data science needs mastery over four different things,
such as statistics, programming, machine learning, and business acumen.

2695
02:54:34,320 --> 02:54:40,356
但如果我告诉你，现在你可以在一年内实现这一目标并成为一名数据科学家呢？
But what if I tell you that now you can attain this feat and become a data scientist within a year?

2696
02:54:40,640 --> 02:54:46,692
如果我告诉你，今天你并不一定需要硕士背景就能成为一名数据科学家呢？
What if I tell you that you don't necessarily need a master's background to become a data scientist today?

2697
02:54:47,182 --> 02:54:53,252
好，朋友们，请耐心看到视频最后，我将回答你如何实现上述两件事。
Well guys, bear with me till the end of this video and I'll answer how you can make the above two things happen.

2698
02:54:53,520 --> 02:55:00,708
通过这个视频，我将为你提供成功的秘诀，也就是能帮助你独立成为数据科学家的路线图。
With this video, I'll provide you with the success mantra, the roadmap that will help you become a data scientist all by yourself.

2699
02:55:01,038 --> 02:55:07,200
但在我们开始之前，请确保订阅并打开 Intellipaat YouTube频道的通知铃铛。
But before we begin, make sure to enable both the subscribe button and bell icon for the Intellipath YouTube channel.

2700
02:55:07,438 --> 02:55:12,160
现在，首先让我们讨论一下为什么你应该考虑从事数据科学职业。
Now, first of all, let's discuss why you should consider a career in data science.

2701
02:55:12,400 --> 02:55:16,932
当涉及到选择职业领域时，你需要回答三个问题。
When it comes to choosing a career domain, you need answers to three questions.

2702
02:55:17,262 --> 02:55:19,680
这个领域目前需求量大吗？
Does the domain have high demand right now?

2703
02:55:19,840 --> 02:55:22,080
它在未来几年还会具有相关性吗？
And will it be relevant in the coming years?

2704
02:55:22,320 --> 02:55:25,280
第二，是否有更好的就业前景？
Number two, are there better job prospects available?

2705
02:55:25,454 --> 02:55:28,640
第三，薪水足够丰厚吗？
Number three, are the salaries lucrative enough?

2706
02:55:28,910 --> 02:55:33,028
好，让我们试着逐一破解这三个问题。
Okay, let's try to break all these three questions one by one.

2707
02:55:33,326 --> 02:55:35,748
首先，我们来谈谈问题一和问题二。
First of all, let's talk about question one and two.

2708
02:55:36,240 --> 02:55:47,360
现在，如果你直接去 Google 搜索现有的数据科学职位，你
会发现仅在 LinkedIn 招聘板上就有超过70万个可用职位。
Right now, if you just go over to the Google search and search for data science jobs available,
you'll get to know that on just the LinkedIn job board, there are 7 lakh plus jobs available.

2709
02:55:47,520 --> 02:55:53,604
如果你考虑到其他的招聘平台，数据科学职位的数量可能还要更多。
If you consider the other job boards, the number of data science jobs available might be even more substantial.

2710
02:55:53,920 --> 02:55:55,440
这是第一点。
Now that's one thing.

2711
02:55:55,680 --> 02:55:56,880
再考虑一下这一点。
Consider this as well.

2712
02:55:57,040 --> 02:56:02,660
在过去的两年里，IT 公司裁减了 400,000 名员工。
In the last two years, 400,000 employees have been laid off by IT companies.

2713
02:56:02,880 --> 02:56:08,720
而且根据 Economic Times 的报道，几乎每个岗位都受到了这些裁员的影响。
And according to the Economic Times report, almost every job was impacted by these layoffs.

2714
02:56:08,910 --> 02:56:13,200
有些岗位受到严重影响，而有些受到的冲击较小。
Some were impacted severely, whereas some faced a less backlash.

2715
02:56:13,360 --> 02:56:19,300
但请看，27% 被裁员的员工来自人力资源背景。
But consider this 27% of laid-off employees were from an HR background.

2716
02:56:19,600 --> 02:56:28,068
22.1% 来自软件开发背景，而来自数据科学背景的人数仅为个位数。
22.1% were from software development background, whereas just single-digit amount of people were from data science backgrounds.

2717
02:56:28,320 --> 02:56:32,388
这意味着 AI 完全没有损害数据科学的就业机会。
What that means is AI did not harm the data science jobs at all.

2718
02:56:33,120 --> 02:56:43,652
此外，由于 AI 和数据科学是相辅相成的，有预测称到本十年末，
这两个领域结合将产生 8000 万个工作岗位。
Also, since both AI and data science go hand in hand, there are predictions that
both the job rules together will produce 80 million jobs by the end of decade ahead.

2719
02:56:43,950 --> 02:56:48,868
这意味着对于数据科学来说，现在和未来都非常光明。
What that means is for data science, both the present and future is quite bright.

2720
02:56:49,120 --> 02:56:51,120
你可能会问，那薪资呢？
What about salaries, you may ask?

2721
02:56:51,280 --> 02:56:56,000
嗯，让我告诉你，数据科学的薪资是 IT 行业最高的之一。
Well, let me tell you that data science salaries are one of the highest in the IT industry.

2722
02:56:56,160 --> 02:57:06,916
即使是初级数据科学家，在印度也能拿到 7 到 19 万卢比的平均薪资，
在美国则是 9.2 万到 20 万美元。
Even the junior data scientist earns an average pay between 7 lakh rupees to 19 lakh rupees in India and 92,000 to 200,000 in the USA.

2723
02:57:07,360 --> 02:57:12,932
你可以看到，数据科学作为一种职业，满足了我们最初设定的所有要求。
You can see that data science as a career clears all the checkboxes that we set out in the beginning.

2724
02:57:13,230 --> 02:57:17,156
因此，数据科学绝对是一个非常好的职业选择。
Hence, definitely data science is a great career option you can go for.

2725
02:57:17,440 --> 02:57:24,560
