例如，假设他们说把 500 名学员放进一个小组，
另外 500 名全部放进另一个小组，全是女性学员。
For example, let's say they said 500 learners we will put into one group or
one batch, and 500 we will put into another batch, all the female learners.

5810
06:19:15,360 --> 06:19:20,240
现在，这能为他们建立高质量的聚类吗？
Right now, is this going to make a good quality cluster for them?

5811
06:19:20,400 --> 06:19:25,280
这对那家公司或者任何地方有帮助吗？
Is it going to be any help to that company or anywhere?

5812
06:19:25,440 --> 06:19:27,120
这会有任何帮助吗？
Is it going to be of any help?

5813
06:19:27,280 --> 06:19:27,812
完全没有。
Not at all.

5814
06:19:28,398 --> 06:19:28,720
没错。
Right.

5815
06:19:28,960 --> 06:19:38,596
因为无论你是把这千人放进一个小组，还是按性别分成两个小组，这都没什么帮助。
Because either you are putting them, those thousand people into one batch, or you are dividing them into on the basis of gender into
two batches, it is not going to be helpful at all.

5816
06:19:39,120 --> 06:19:47,684
仅凭这一个因素，似乎是把这千个数据点分成两组的一个非常糟糕的因素。
This one factor alone does seem to be a very bad factor to divide these thousand data points into two groups.

5817
06:19:48,526 --> 06:19:49,028
正确。
Correct.

5818
06:19:49,582 --> 06:19:56,260
假设我换一个因素，比如我们不用性别，而是用学员的领域。
Let's say if I take another factor, let's say we don't use the gender, rather, we use the domain of the learners.

5819
06:19:56,974 --> 06:20:07,684
现在，如果我把这个因素从性别改为领域，这会是把这些学员分成小组更好的因素吗？
Now, if I change this this factor from the gender to this domain,
will that be a much better factor to divide these learners into groups?

5820
06:20:08,398 --> 06:20:09,840
它会是更好的因素吗？
Will it be a much better factor?

5821
06:20:10,000 --> 06:20:21,764
当然，它会是更好的因素，因为现在，如果千名学员被分成 IT 组，那些属于 IT 领域的，
以及那些不属于 IT 领域的非 IT 领域。
Of course, it will be a much better factor because now, if thousand learners are divided into batches of IT,
those who belong to IT domain and those who not who belong to non-IT domain.

5822
06:20:22,160 --> 06:20:34,404
在这种情况下，Intellipad 将能够更好地服务学员，因为他们知道这些学员该如何被教学，
以及根据他们掌握的技术知识多少来决定教学方式。
then in that case, Intellipad will be able to serve the learners in a better way because they know how these learners have to be
taught and how these learners have to be taught, how much technical things they know on the basis of that.

5823
06:20:35,086 --> 06:20:43,364
所以，我想向你们展示的是，可以有多个因素来建立小组，但并非所有因素都足够好。
So, what I'm trying to show you here that there can be multiple factors on the
basis of which you can make groups, but all the factors are not good enough.

5824
06:20:44,080 --> 06:20:50,052
就像在监督学习中，并不是所有的输入列对于预测输出都同样重要。
Like in the supervised learning, all the input columns are not equally important to predict the output.

5825
06:20:50,240 --> 06:20:54,116
有些列非常重要，而有些列就没那么重要。
There will be some very important columns and there will be some very less important.

5826
06:20:54,734 --> 06:21:01,860
同样地，我们可以有多个因素，但每个因素对于建立小组来说并不都同样重要。
Same way, we can have multiple factors, and every factor will not be equally important for making the groups.

5827
06:21:02,254 --> 06:21:05,444
有些非常重要，有些就没那么重要。
Some will be very much important, some will be very less important.

5828
06:21:07,054 --> 06:21:11,044
如果我不只取单个因素，而是把两个因素合并成一个呢？
If instead of taking single single factor, what if I combine two into one?

5829
06:21:11,598 --> 06:21:15,716
假设我取 IT 和非 IT，这给了我非常好的聚类。
Let's say I took IT non-IT, that gave me very good cluster.

5830
06:21:15,920 --> 06:21:18,628
但如果我取两个因素呢？
But what if I take two of the factors?

5831
06:21:18,990 --> 06:21:21,540
假设是他们的经验水平和领域。
Let's say their experience level and domain.

5832
06:21:22,318 --> 06:21:31,076
所以我可以建立四个小组：职场新人 IT、职场新人非
IT、有经验的 IT 领域学员、有经验的非 IT 领域学员。
So one group I make fresher IT, fresher non-IT, experience of IT domain, experience learners from non-IT domain.

5833
06:21:31,680 --> 06:21:43,940
如果我根据这两个因素建立这四个小组，我可以看到小组
的质量因为采用了这两个非常好的分组因素而大幅提升。
If I have these four groups on the basis of these two factors, I can see the quality of the group increasing much just because of
taking these two factors, which are very good factors of making the groups.

5834
06:21:44,686 --> 06:21:55,204
通过这种方式，你就能理解，每当你要做这种无监督学习任务时，你不需要考虑所有的因素。
And that way you are understanding that whenever you have to do this kind
of unsupervised learning task, then all the factors you don't have to take.

5835
06:21:55,534 --> 06:22:06,180
你必须清楚地理解，在给定的，比如说 50 个输入列、50 个输入因素中，
哪些输入因素是足够好的，可以用来建立小组。
You have to clearly understand out of given, let's say, 50 input columns, 50 input factors,
which of the input factors are good enough to make the groups.

5836
06:22:06,574 --> 06:22:17,060
所以从 50 个输入列中，你可以只选出 10 个或 12 个看
起来最重要的，然后完全舍弃剩下的，来划分最终的聚类。
So out of 50 input columns, you can just use 10 of them or 12 of them, which seems to be the most important one,
and you can discard totally the rest of them for making the final groups.

5837
06:22:17,838 --> 06:22:18,240
对。
Right.

5838
06:22:18,510 --> 06:22:21,956
这是一个持续的实验过程。
And this is an ongoing experimental process.

5839
06:22:22,670 --> 06:22:29,668
在这种情况下，很难一下子找出那 10 到 12 个对你最有帮助的输入列。
In this case, it is very difficult to identify those 10, 12 input columns, which will be very helpful for you.

5840
06:22:30,000 --> 06:22:36,164
所以这类任务不是在两个月、三个月或四个月内就能解决的。
So this kind of task is not solved in let's say two months, three months, four months.

5841
06:22:36,480 --> 06:22:38,852
这类任务可能会持续好几年。
This kind of task goes on for years.

5842
06:22:39,534 --> 06:22:43,364
所以你会先尝试 10 个，然后试个六个月。
So you will be trying 10 first, then you try that for six months.

5843
06:22:43,662 --> 06:22:46,756
接着再选另外 10 个特征，再试个六个月。
Then you pick another 10 features, you try that for another six months.

5844
06:22:47,246 --> 06:22:56,240
经过多次尝试，你最终会找到那 10 到 12 个或 15 个能给你带来最佳结果的特征。
So after multiple trying, you will be finding out those 10, 12, or 15 features that were giving you the best result.

5845
06:22:56,622 --> 06:22:56,880
对。
Right.

5846
06:22:57,230 --> 06:23:05,380
当你利用这些因素把客户分成这么多组时，你就能划分出非常高质量的聚类。
When you divided the customers into that many groups, taking those factors, you were able to make very good quality groups.

5847
06:23:05,838 --> 06:23:09,988
那我们通过划分这些高质量聚类，能得到什么好处呢？
And what we do by making those good quality groups, what is the benefit?

5848
06:23:10,382 --> 06:23:14,880
首先，好处是公司将能够……嗯，对。
First, the benefit is that a company will be able to um right.

5849
06:23:15,120 --> 06:23:21,840
如果公司划分出了高质量的聚类，他们就能更好地服务这些客户，对吧？
A company will be able to serve those customers better if they have made good quality clusters, right?

5850
06:23:22,080 --> 06:23:30,240
其次，你看如果 Amazon 把客户分成了多个组，对吧？
And Second, you see that if the Amazon has divided the customers into multiple groups, right?

5851
06:23:30,670 --> 06:23:36,452
他们知道其中一组是那种年轻人但消费较低的人。
They know that one group is that kind of people who are young but less spenders.

5852
06:23:36,910 --> 06:23:40,260
而另一组是那些年轻且高消费的客户。
And one group is those customers who are young but high spenders.

5853
06:23:40,654 --> 06:23:44,964
这样 Amazon 就可以进行非常精准的定向营销。
So Amazon can do a very proper targeted marketing.

5854
06:23:45,326 --> 06:23:50,852
任何公司都可以根据他们掌握的信息进行精准的定向营销。
Any company can do a proper targeted marketing on the basis of those things that they know.

5855
06:23:51,598 --> 06:23:53,060
定向营销是什么？
Targeted marketing was what?

5856
06:23:53,440 --> 06:23:59,172
假设 Amazon 正在搞促销或者有任何优惠活动。
If let's say Amazon has some sale going on or they have any offer going on.

5857
06:23:59,840 --> 06:24:06,340
现在他们需要向某些客户发送关于该优惠或促销的通知。
Now they have to send notification about that offer or sale to some customers.

5858
06:24:07,054 --> 06:24:16,900
现在，每当你安装了 Amazon 应用时，你都会收到 Flipkart、
Amazon 或任何你安装过的应用的很多通知。
Now, whenever you have your Amazon app installed, you will be getting a lot of notifications of Flipkart, Amazon,
any any of these applications that you have installed.

5859
06:24:17,120 --> 06:24:22,308
也就是说，任何销售美容产品或健康相关产品的初创公司。
Any means any startup who is selling some, let's say, beauty products or health-related products.

5860
06:24:22,606 --> 06:24:27,044
如果你也安装了它们的应用，你就会在智能手机上收到关于优惠的通知。
That also, if you have installed, you'll be getting notifications about the offer on your smartphone.

5861
06:24:27,886 --> 06:24:32,900
但是，同样的通知、同样的优惠并不是发给所有客户的。
Now, the same notification, same offer is not being sent to all the customers of that.

5862
06:24:33,742 --> 06:24:40,960
你会收到非常特定类型的通知，这会促使你花更多的钱，对吧？
You are being sent a very specific type of notification, which makes you spend more, right?

5863
06:24:41,120 --> 06:24:46,372
这会促使你购买正在向你推销的那件产品。
Which makes you purchase that product which is being sold to you.

5864
06:24:47,118 --> 06:24:47,520
对。
Right.

5865
06:24:47,726 --> 06:24:50,180
这就是所谓的定向营销。
And this is known as a targeted marketing.

5866
06:24:50,720 --> 06:24:57,252
所以如果这些公司知道你是哪种类型的客户，他们就能更好地对你进行定向营销。
So if those companies know what kind of customer you are, then they will be able to target you better.

5867
06:24:57,550 --> 06:25:01,600
所以这个群体里的所有人都是年轻人，而且消费能力都很强。
So all the people who are in this group, they are all young and high spenders.

5868
06:25:01,806 --> 06:25:03,204
他们喜欢高消费，而且他们很年轻。
They like to spend high, they are young.

5869
06:25:03,534 --> 06:25:10,852
所以他们必须收到这类通知，从而促使他们购买这类产品。
So they have to be sent those kind of notifications which will make them purchase those kind of products.

5870
06:25:11,246 --> 06:25:22,320
比如任何即将推出的时尚产品，或者任何新款智能手机，
他们就是喜欢这类产品且有能力支付这么多钱的人。
So about any fashion product which is coming up, about any new smartphone which is coming up,
and they are the people who like those kind of products and they're capable of spending that much.

5871
06:25:22,638 --> 06:25:22,880
没错。
Correct.

5872
06:25:22,960 --> 06:25:27,780
所以他们会收到这些通知，从而促使这些人购买那个商品。
So they will be sent those notifications which will make these people purchase that item.

5873
06:25:28,622 --> 06:25:35,108
所以定向营销是无监督学习最著名的应用之一。
So targeted marketing is one of the most famous kind of application of unsupervised learning.

5874
06:25:35,726 --> 06:25:41,508
首先，公司会将所有客户分成不同的群体，然后他们会用不同的方式来服务这些客户。
So first the companies will divide all the customers into group, then they will be serving them in different ways.

5875
06:25:42,670 --> 06:25:48,996
其次，无监督学习的第二个非常著名的例子就是推荐系统。
Second, the second very famous example of this unsupervised learning is recommendation systems.

5876
06:25:49,550 --> 06:25:52,580
推荐系统现在非常出名。
Recommendation systems is a very famous thing now.

5877
06:25:52,880 --> 06:26:00,388
它已经在市场上存在了10年，并且到目前为止已经得到了极大的改进。
It is there in the market from last 10 years and it has improved to a very good extent as of now.

5878
06:26:01,166 --> 06:26:02,640
推荐系统是什么？
The recommendation systems are what?

5879
06:26:02,880 --> 06:26:13,860
当你访问任何网站寻找产品时，当你向下滚动同一个产品页面时，
你会看到系统向你推荐其他与该产品相似的商品。
When you go on any website and you're looking for a product, as you scroll down on the same page of that product,
you'll see other items being recommended to you, which are similar to that product.

5880
06:26:14,670 --> 06:26:17,200
所以，系统是怎么向你推荐东西的，对吧？
So, how something is being recommended to you, right?

5881
06:26:17,280 --> 06:26:18,084
是基于什么基础的？
On what basis?

5882
06:26:18,894 --> 06:26:23,920
在现实世界的市场中，有两种类型的推荐系统在运行。
So there are two types of recommendation systems that work in the real world market.

5883
06:26:24,142 --> 06:26:28,164
两种类型：协同过滤和基于内容的过滤。
Two types: collaborative filtering, content-based filtering.

5884
06:26:28,480 --> 06:26:28,880
没错。
Correct.

5885
06:26:28,960 --> 06:26:33,284
而且随着课程的推进，我想你会做一个关于这个推荐系统的项目。
And you will be making uh, I think, a project of this recommendation system as you move forward.

5886
06:26:34,080 --> 06:26:38,372
所以，推荐系统分为两种：协同过滤和基于内容的过滤。
So, recommendation systems are of two types collaborative, content-based.

5887
06:26:38,560 --> 06:26:46,372
而且推荐系统只是无监督学习的一种应用，也就是你到目前为止每天都在使用的东西。
And recommendation systems are an application of unsupervised learning only that you have been using on a day-to-day basis till now.

5888
06:26:47,534 --> 06:26:49,092
那么，什么是协同过滤？
So, what is collaborative filtering?

5889
06:26:49,600 --> 06:26:52,580
在协同过滤中，情况是这样的。
In collaborative filtering, this kind of thing happens.

5890
06:26:53,198 --> 06:27:00,100
假设这是用户1，这是用户2，这两个人都在同一个群体里，因为他们是相似类型的客户。
Let's say that this is person one, this is person two, and these both
people are in the same group because these are similar type of customers.

5891
06:27:00,654 --> 06:27:01,668
公司知道这一点。
The company knows that.

5892
06:27:02,478 --> 06:27:04,964
即这两个客户都在同一个群体里。
That these are both the customers in the same group.

5893
06:27:05,600 --> 06:27:14,436
现在假设用户1从Amazon、Flipkart或者Walmart等公司购买了一件T恤。
And now let's say this person one purchases a t shirt from that company Amazon, Flipkart, whatever, Walmart, anything.

5894
06:27:15,566 --> 06:27:20,320
假设这个人进入那个平台，购买了一件T恤。
So let's say this person goes onto that platform, purchases a t shirt.

5895
06:27:21,582 --> 06:27:26,436
现在，公司知道这个人也是与此非常相似的客户类型。
Now, the company knows that this person is also very similar type of customer to this.

5896
06:27:27,150 --> 06:27:33,856
所以，当这个人打开那个应用程序时，他们的主页也会推荐这件 T 恤。
So, this person too will also be recommended this t-shirt on their home page when they open that application.

5897
06:27:34,016 --> 06:27:36,516
他们会在某个地方看到这个商品的推荐。
Somewhere they will be recommended this item.

5898
06:27:37,262 --> 06:27:47,076
为什么要给这个人推荐这个商品呢？因为既然他们是相似类型的客户，
他们可能在某些方面有相似的喜好。
And why this item is being recommended to this person in the hope that since these are similar type of customers,
they might have similar type of likes somewhat or the other.

5899
06:27:47,758 --> 06:28:00,772
如果我们向他们推荐这件 T 恤，他们购买这件 T 恤的可能性就比购买其他 T 恤要高；
或者如果我们推荐其他产品，他们可能不太喜欢那些产品。
And this person too will be more likely to purchase this t-shirt compared to any other t-shirt if we recommend them,
or compared to any other product if we recommend them, there are low chances that this person might like them.

5900
06:28:01,198 --> 06:28:04,196
因为我们不知道这个人的真实喜好是什么。
Because we don't know what is the actual liking of this person.

5901
06:28:04,846 --> 06:28:15,056
但如果第一个人喜欢这件 T 恤，而同样这件 T 恤被推荐给第二个人，
那么第二个人购买它的可能性就非常高。
But if person one likes this t-shirt, the same t-shirt, if that is being recommended to person two,
there are very high chances that this person two will purchase that.

5902
06:28:15,566 --> 06:28:26,116
现在，这个群体里还有其他人，比如第三个人、第四个人、第五个人，还有很多其他客户，
成千上万甚至数百万客户都在这个群体里。
Now, in this group, there will be other people also person three, person four, person five, lot of other customers are there,
thousands, even millions of customers are there in a group.

5903
06:28:26,510 --> 06:28:34,852
所以，如果你收到了某种产品的推荐，一方面可能
是基于你的搜索历史，也就是你喜欢什么样的东西。
So if you are being recommended any type of product, one, it can be on the basis of your search history, what kind of thing you like.

5904
06:28:35,342 --> 06:28:45,252
但除此之外，你看到的很多推荐是基于其他与你非常相似的客户购买了什么。
But apart from that, a lot of recommendations you are seeing is on the basis
of what other type of other customers purchased, which are very similar to you.

5905
06:28:45,966 --> 06:28:46,468
没错。
Correct.

5906
06:28:46,736 --> 06:28:49,764
这就是协同过滤的概念。
That is the concept of collaborative filtering.

5907
06:28:50,350 --> 06:28:52,964
第二个被称为基于内容的过滤。
The second one is known as content-based filtering.

5908
06:28:54,126 --> 06:29:01,696
基于内容的过滤在 Netflix、YouTube 和 Hotstar 上非常常见。
The content-based filtering happens very famously on Netflix, YouTube, Hotstar.

5909
06:29:02,712 --> 06:29:02,732
对吧？
right?

5910
06:29:03,136 --> 06:29:08,176
在这些平台上，你会看到大量的基于内容的过滤。
These content-based platforms where you see this content-based filtering happens very much on those.

5911
06:29:08,430 --> 06:29:13,456
是的，在 Instagram、Facebook、Snapchat，显然在这些社交媒体平台上也是如此。
Yeah, on Instagram, Facebook, Snapchat, obviously, in those social media platforms also.

5912
06:29:13,776 --> 06:29:14,816
什么是基于内容的过滤？
What is content-based?

5913
06:29:14,976 --> 06:29:28,388
基于内容的过滤就是，嗯，举个例子，如果我谈到 Amazon，
如果第一个人喜欢这款智能手机并正在查看它，或者他们已经把这款智能手机加入购物车了。
Content-based is nothing but um, for example, if I talk about Amazon, so if person one likes this smartphone and they are looking at
that, or they have added this smartphone one into their cart.

5914
06:29:29,422 --> 06:29:36,868
那么，这款智能手机二也会被推荐给第一个人，因为这两款智能手机现在属于同一个组。
Now, this smartphone two will be also recommended to this person one because these both the smartphones are in one group now.

5915
06:29:37,614 --> 06:29:43,684
所以在这种情况下，人不在一个组里，而是设备、产品在同一个组里。
So in this case, the people are not in a group, but now the devices, the products are in a group.

5916
06:29:44,430 --> 06:29:51,684
所以如果这个人喜欢这个商品，他们可能也会喜欢那个商品，因为这两个商品非常相似。
So if this person like this item, so this person might also like this item because these two items are very similar to each other.

5917
